/* UniPath — bachelor's degrees conferred by discipline area.
   Source: section J of each institution's Common Data Set ("Disciplinary areas
   of DEGREES CONFERRED"), read from the official document linked in `source`.
   `areas` holds the Bachelor's column exactly as published: a percentage of
   bachelor's degrees (unit "percent") or a number of degrees (unit "count").
   Categories with no figure are left out. `period` is the July–June year the
   degrees were conferred in; `checked` is the day the document was read.

   How the site uses it (UNIPATH.applyLayers in data/registry.js):
   - a field tag stays on a record when at least one of its categories
     (UNIPATH.fieldAreas) has degrees, or when UNIPATH.fieldNotes records an
     official page that lists a major;
   - a field tag with no degrees and no such page is taken off the record and
     listed on the profile with the reason;
   - a field with at least 1% of bachelor's degrees is added as a tag.
   Economics is not a category of its own in the Common Data Set — it is
   counted inside "Social sciences" — so that tag cannot be checked this way.
   Institutions that are not listed here have not been checked. */
